Package: chokepointR
Type: Package
Title: Global Trade Chokepoint Risks and Resilience
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R:
    person("Thierry", "Warin", , "thierry.warin@hec.ca", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5921-3428"))
Description: Profiles the disruption risk and resilience of the world's major
    maritime trade chokepoints -- the eight straits and canals through which a
    large share of seaborne trade and oil must pass. For each chokepoint it
    combines how much world trade depends on it, route substitutability, a panel
    of graph-theory centrality indicators (weighted and unweighted betweenness,
    degree and weighted strength, harmonic centrality and PageRank) computed on
    the country-chokepoint trade-dependency network, quantitative traffic and
    cargo context (vessel transits, vessel and cargo mix, trade shares, local
    economic dependence), documented disruption incidents (2018 onward, each with
    a resolvable citation), and composite resilience and vulnerability indices, to
    support assessment of how exposed supply chains and global value chains are to
    trade-route disruption. Every quantitative figure carries a per-cell source,
    URL and confidence flag. Trade-dependency, systemic-risk and centrality
    measures build on Verschuur and Hall (2025) <doi:10.5281/zenodo.13841881>;
    oil-transit figures are from the U.S. Energy Information Administration. An
    optional helper queries a live hazard feed (USGS) without redistributing
    third-party data.
